WEBVTT

00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:08.110
It's Tonegawa.

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:11.860
You called for me, sir?

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:18.070
There you are, Tonegawa.

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:18.950
Show him.

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:19.640
Yes, sir.

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:26.250
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:32.380
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:35.890
What do you think, Tonegawa?

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:40.390
What do I think? About what?

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:46.360
<i>A bug... A baseball... Youth? Summer?</i>

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:53.320
Are these mementos of a childhood summer?

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:55.780
Someone is out to get me.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:57.160
They're after my life.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:59.510
Y-Your life?

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:02.660
Three days ago...

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:06.670
Look out!

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:12.460
Sorry about that!

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:15.790
And then yesterday...

00:01:15.790 --> 00:01:19.100
President! There's a hornet on your back!

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:24.350
They're clever bastards, I'll give them that!

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:29.260
Thinking back, that must be why 
I almost tripped last week, too...

00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:30.630
<i>This is...</i>

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:32.360
<i>Tonegawa came to a realization.</i>

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:36.740
<i>This is just a string of minor 
bad luck resulting in...</i>

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:39.240
<b>Persecution complex!!</b>

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:39.240
<i>a persecution complex!</i>

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:44.860
That being the case, Tonegawa, 
I assume you know what I'm asking of you.

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:47.610
Of course! I'll assign additional security—

00:01:46.550 --> 00:01:48.250
A decoy!

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:52.470
You will find a body double 
who is my exact twin!

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:57.010
<i>A decoy?!</i>

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:07.100
<b>Middle Management Blues</b>

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:07.100
<b><i>Mr. Tonegawa</i></b>

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:32.210
<i>Thus, due to President Hyoudou's 
overwhelming persecution complex,</i>

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:32.660
<i>Agenda 12
</i>Fake

00:03:32.210 --> 00:03:34.220
<i>Team Tonegawa begins...</i>

00:03:34.220 --> 00:03:35.210
Go find him!

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:35.980
Yes, sir!

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:37.980
<b>The manhunt for the president's identical twin!</b>

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:40.490
<i>...the manhunt for the 
president's identical twin!</i>

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:41.490
Looking for this man!

00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:42.740
<i>However...</i>

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:47.990
<i>All of the candidates are 
slightly off. Not quite there.</i>

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:47.990
Student ID
Name: Todou Kazumasa
Department: General Education 
Date of Birth: 19XX/12/1X
Blood Type: O
This ID confirms the above individual is a student at this school.

00:03:52.820 --> 00:03:55.600
We still haven't found anyone 
who looks exactly like him.

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:56.590
Yeah.

00:03:56.590 --> 00:04:01.260
Could someone who looks like 
the president really even exist?

00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:03.970
Fool! Don't say that!

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:07.070
But, sir, think of his nose!

00:04:07.070 --> 00:04:09.330
If you look from the front, 
it's clearly rounded,

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:09.490
Rounded

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:11.290
but from the side, it's so angular!

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:12.230
Angular

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:13.540
How does that work, 
three-dimensionally speaking?!

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:15.230
He'd be impossible to make a figurine of!

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:17.420
There can't be anyone who looks like that!

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:19.500
Easy there, Yamazaki.

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:23.860
<b>Organic Dining: Kisara</b>

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:23.860
For now, let's grab a bite to eat.

00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:31.610
Excuse me! We're ready to order.

00:04:31.610 --> 00:04:32.870
Oh, certainly.

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:34.900
Table 3 is ready to order.

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:35.750
Coming!

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:41.360
Hello there. Sorry about the wait.

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:43.340
Yeah, could I get the—

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:56.830
T-Tonegawa-sensei!

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:02.930
<i>Such an overwhelming resemblance!</i>

00:05:02.930 --> 00:05:04.930
<i>He looks like the president from every angle!</i>

00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:07.430
<i>Even the shape of his nose is perfect!</i>

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:09.990
<i>What a fortuitous turn!</i>

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:09.990
<b>Fortune</b>

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:11.880
Um, can I take your order?

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:13.240
Oh, r-right...

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:16.240
Two stir-fried meat and vegetable meals.

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:17.250
Sure thing.

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:20.470
Here you go.

00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:22.470
Eat up while it's warm, now.

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:26.170
R-Right. Thanks for the food.

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:43.530
Tonegawa-sensei...

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:46.110
Yes, it's quite good.

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:47.110
Sweet, isn't it?

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:50.220
We only use 100% organic ingredients.

00:05:49.090 --> 00:05:50.870
100%

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:50.870
<b>Organic!</b>

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:53.620
What do you think it's seasoned with?

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:56.870
Get this... It's just salt!

00:05:56.870 --> 00:05:59.630
That's the best way to bring 
the ingredients to... huh?

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:10.640
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:06:02.390 --> 00:06:05.020
You folks don't seem too surprised.

00:06:05.480 --> 00:06:07.580
Are you tired or something?

00:06:11.380 --> 00:06:13.140
Things rough at work?

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:15.640
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:19.740
<i>It was a string of phrases they couldn't 
imagine from President Hyoudou,</i>

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:19.290
<b>The world</b>

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:23.080
<i>even if the world was turned upside-down!</i>

00:06:23.970 --> 00:06:27.420
<i>To put it in simple terms... 
he sounds like a fake!</i>

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:28.150
<b>Fake</b>

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:31.920
<i>He definitely bears a perfect resemblance.</i>

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:33.730
<i>He does, and yet...</i>

00:06:33.730 --> 00:06:37.660
100% organic. Are you tired or something?

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:39.460
Things rough at work?

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:42.470
<i>But, no! Their personalities 
are totally different!</i>

00:06:42.470 --> 00:06:46.000
Tonegawa-sensei, let's go with him.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:47.140
But...

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:48.050
It's okay, sir.

00:06:48.690 --> 00:06:50.810
As one who once worked 
directly underneath him,

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:54.560
I have seen his mannerisms, his habits, 
and his way of speaking firsthand.

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:57.960
Let's whip him into shape,

00:06:57.960 --> 00:07:00.560
so he acts as much like 
the president as he looks!

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:08.050
<b>Twenty days after the 
president's order...</b>

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:06.750
<i>Twenty days after the president's order...</i>

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:10.500
<i>He is finally found!</i>

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:13.570
<i>The diabolically identical 
doppelganger: Honda Masayasu!</i>

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:18.330
So basically, I'm supposed to act as 
a stand-in for this Hyoudou-san?

00:07:14.090 --> 00:07:18.330
<b>Diabolically
identical
doppelganger!</b>

00:07:14.090 --> 00:07:18.330
<b>Honda Masayasu</b>

00:07:18.690 --> 00:07:21.020
Yes, that's right.

00:07:21.530 --> 00:07:23.540
Of course, you'd be provided 
with boarding and meals.

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:25.480
That sounds like a great offer, but...

00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:27.590
Please! You'd be doing us a huge favor!

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:33.590
Go on, Masayan.

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:35.610
B-But boss...

00:07:35.610 --> 00:07:36.890
Never you mind, just go!

00:07:37.240 --> 00:07:39.890
You've never been able to turn down 
someone in need, have you?

00:07:41.050 --> 00:07:43.880
You really have me all figured out...

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:49.280
Okay, you've got it! 
Leave everything to good ol' Masayan!

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:52.280
Yeah, yeah!

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:54.780
<i>And thus...</i>

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:58.060
<i>Masayan is transported to Teiai!</i>

00:07:59.860 --> 00:08:02.690
This is your personal room, Masayan-sama.

00:08:02.690 --> 00:08:04.170
Yahoo!

00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:10.630
Wow, I feel a bit guilty, 
getting my own private...

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:12.490
room?

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:23.690
Uh, um, say...

00:08:23.690 --> 00:08:25.800
Well, Yamazaki, you can take it from here.

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:26.190
Yes, sir!

00:08:26.720 --> 00:08:29.970
I will take responsibility for molding him

00:08:29.970 --> 00:08:33.280
into our dark, twisted president!

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:36.070
Wait, "dark" and "twisted"?

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:40.090
Uh, Yamazaki-san, what exactly are we—

00:08:40.090 --> 00:08:40.830
Wrong!

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:45.580
The president doesn't remember 
the names of men in black! Ever!

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:45.580
<b>Ever!</b>

00:08:46.650 --> 00:08:48.280
When you call for me,

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:51.060
it's "Hey!" "Pointy-chin!" Or "Sunglasses!"

00:08:51.060 --> 00:08:52.680
Sir, I could never—

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:54.220
Nobody is called sir...

00:08:54.790 --> 00:08:56.410
Except you!

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:03.420
We've already begun the special 
training to turn you into the president!

00:09:05.220 --> 00:09:06.350
<i>It begins.</i>

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:08.230
Punishment.

00:09:08.820 --> 00:09:10.750
Punishment. Take your punishment...

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:12.150
You're swinging too slow!

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:13.940
Faster! With a smoother motion!

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:17.240
<i>Yamazaki unleashes a harsh and unrelenting</i>

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:17.240
<b>Harsh!</b>

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:17.240
<b>Unrelenting!</b>

00:09:17.610 --> 00:09:19.750
<i>disciplinary education session!</i>

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:19.750
<b>Strict Education!</b>

00:09:20.230 --> 00:09:21.320
Thank you for the—

00:09:21.320 --> 00:09:22.660
Stop right there!

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:25.250
You've already made three mistakes.

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:27.060
One!

00:09:27.060 --> 00:09:30.500
The president never thanks 
anyone for anything!

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:33.930
Two! He doesn't use a knife and fork!

00:09:35.560 --> 00:09:37.380
All food is finger food!

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:39.260
And third!

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:44.020
The president... is almost always drooling!

00:09:52.020 --> 00:10:00.780
Regarding President Hyoudou's Laughter
(Cackling)

00:09:52.550 --> 00:09:56.370
The president's laughter, 
90% of the time, is a kind of cackle.

00:09:55.900 --> 00:09:56.970
<b>Kah kah kah!</b>

00:09:56.370 --> 00:10:00.790
"Kah kah kah!" Or "Kuh kuh kuh!" 
Or alternatively, "Guh huh huh..."

00:09:57.070 --> 00:09:58.010
<b>Kuh kuh kuh...</b>

00:09:58.820 --> 00:09:59.800
<b>Guh huh huh</b>

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:04.220
"Kah kah kah" and "kuh kuh kuh"...

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:06.310
And alternately...

00:10:06.310 --> 00:10:08.290
And now, right in front of you...

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:11.180
stands a debtor who is suffering 
and writhing in agony.

00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:13.690
What's your reaction, President?!

00:10:16.100 --> 00:10:18.000
Kah... kah kah kah!

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:19.220
Wrong!

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:21.720
In this situation, it's "Kee kee kee!"

00:10:20.530 --> 00:10:21.720
<b>Kee Kee Kee</b>

00:10:22.130 --> 00:10:23.770
Kee... kee kee kee!

00:10:23.770 --> 00:10:24.470
Again!

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:26.160
More diabolically!

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:27.260
Kee kee kee!

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:28.620
With more drool!

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:29.730
Kee kee kee!

00:10:30.930 --> 00:10:32.710
How's it going?

00:10:32.710 --> 00:10:33.690
Well, sir...

00:10:33.690 --> 00:10:38.570
He hasn't quite fully committed yet, 
so he still has a long way to go,

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:44.080
but occasionally, it shocks me how 
much he resembles the genuine article.

00:10:46.570 --> 00:10:48.430
He definitely has the raw potential.

00:10:48.930 --> 00:10:55.800
I think we might have found 
an incredible body double.

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:05.020
Things rough at work?

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:09.830
Punishment!

00:11:09.830 --> 00:11:14.820
Punishment! 
Take your punishment! Punishment!

00:11:11.960 --> 00:11:14.820
No, no! That's all wrong!

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:18.190
The real president is more diabolical!

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:18.190
<b>Diabolical!</b>

00:11:19.410 --> 00:11:21.140
Not a "whap," but a "crack"!

00:11:21.140 --> 00:11:22.040
Crack...

00:11:22.040 --> 00:11:24.970
How many times must I say it?! 
Are you even taking this seriously?!

00:11:25.180 --> 00:11:27.690
You fail at everything you do!

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:30.910
We brought you in because 
you resembled the president,

00:11:30.910 --> 00:11:33.880
but the bottom line is... 
you're a spineless wimp!

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:38.060
Spineless! Spineless! Spineless!

00:11:38.060 --> 00:11:41.300
I'm... I'm...

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:45.430
not a spineless wimp!

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:51.110
Th-That felt... as smooth as a horse's tail!

00:11:51.110 --> 00:11:54.390
That's right. Don't forget that feeling.

00:11:54.390 --> 00:11:56.310
W-Wait, were you...

00:11:57.050 --> 00:12:00.440
The president's punishment is, 
in essence, his rage!

00:12:01.270 --> 00:12:04.700
He metes out abuse with 
his rage! He punishes!

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:04.700
<b>Rage!</b>

00:12:02.820 --> 00:12:04.700
<b>Abuse!</b>

00:12:05.540 --> 00:12:08.470
I didn't think you'd come 
so far in such a short time.

00:12:08.470 --> 00:12:10.450
Well, thank you...

00:12:10.840 --> 00:12:13.210
All right, that's it for today.

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:16.650
I've burned a few CDs with the 
president's laughter on them.

00:12:16.520 --> 00:12:18.960
Happiness

00:12:16.520 --> 00:12:18.960
Intoxication

00:12:16.520 --> 00:12:18.960
Ecstasy

00:12:16.650 --> 00:12:18.450
Go over them before bed tonight.

00:12:18.450 --> 00:12:18.960
Got it!

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:21.670
<i>Then, one month later...</i>

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:23.490
<b>One month later...</b>

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:23.970
Come on in, Tonegawa-sensei.

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:32.970
There you are, Tonegawa.

00:12:32.970 --> 00:12:35.260
M-Masayan?!

00:12:36.920 --> 00:12:40.250
It's not just his looks anymore. 
His voice, mannerisms, word choice,

00:12:40.250 --> 00:12:43.870
and even his thinking have been 
modeled to match the president's.

00:12:44.370 --> 00:12:48.870
No, I'd say that now, he's more like 
the president than the president himself.

00:12:48.870 --> 00:12:52.330
He might be more authentic than the original!

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:55.370
President, your meal is ready.

00:12:56.790 --> 00:12:58.000
Enjoy.

00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:00.250
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:03.500
Wait, Yamazaki, that's still too hot...

00:13:08.470 --> 00:13:11.480
He ate it as is?!

00:13:12.570 --> 00:13:16.680
I'm honestly unsure if it was 
necessary to take it this far,

00:13:16.680 --> 00:13:18.580
but you've done remarkable work, Yamazaki.

00:13:18.580 --> 00:13:20.250
Thank you, sir.

00:13:20.250 --> 00:13:21.880
<i>For better or worse,</i>

00:13:21.880 --> 00:13:26.240
<i>the body double project comes to a 
successful completion after two months!</i>

00:13:27.060 --> 00:13:31.990
<i>An overwhelmingly authentic 
decoy, Masayan, has arrived!</i>

00:13:32.340 --> 00:13:34.000
<i>And the next day...</i>

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:37.100
It's Tonegawa.

00:13:39.940 --> 00:13:42.250
You called for me, sir?

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:44.210
Tonegawa.

00:13:44.210 --> 00:13:46.760
Do you know why I called you here?

00:13:47.150 --> 00:13:50.840
Yes, of course. The body double that you—

00:13:50.840 --> 00:13:52.260
Then let's get down to it.

00:13:57.270 --> 00:13:59.520
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:14:00.200 --> 00:14:02.040
Please take a card.

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:07.210
You've got your card, then, Tonegawa?

00:14:07.210 --> 00:14:08.280
Y-Yes, sir.

00:14:10.610 --> 00:14:12.780
I can hear it, I can hear it...

00:14:12.780 --> 00:14:17.740
The more you try to hide it, the louder 
the voice of your mind becomes.

00:14:17.740 --> 00:14:21.410
The card you chose was...

00:14:21.410 --> 00:14:23.310
the triangle!

00:14:25.380 --> 00:14:27.900
<i>Does this mean...</i>

00:14:27.690 --> 00:14:35.120
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:14:30.600 --> 00:14:33.690
<i>Tonegawa has a bad feeling already.</i>

00:14:33.690 --> 00:14:35.730
<i>No, more than a bad feeling...</i>

00:14:35.730 --> 00:14:38.070
Well? I got you, didn't I?

00:14:38.070 --> 00:14:39.140
<i>A bad certainty!</i>

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:44.650
<b>Mentalism</b>

00:14:40.010 --> 00:14:44.650
<i>The president's interest in having 
a body double is already long gone!</i>

00:14:45.430 --> 00:14:49.150
<i>The effort of Tonegawa and his 
project amounts to nothing!</i>

00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:52.160
<b>Masayan</b>

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:54.460
Th-That can't be!

00:14:54.460 --> 00:14:56.080
What happens to Masayan, then?!

00:14:57.050 --> 00:15:00.330
Yamazaki, I hate to say it, but 
we can't keep looking after him.

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:05.560
But... Masayan, is...

00:15:07.780 --> 00:15:10.180
Pardon me, Tonegawa-san.

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:12.800
I've got the papers you asked for...

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:18.810
Wow. Is that the body double you mentioned?

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:20.790
Yes, he is, but...

00:15:20.790 --> 00:15:22.360
it turns out...

00:15:24.760 --> 00:15:27.960
So the mood's already shifted? 
That is bad news.

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:28.690
Yeah...

00:15:29.010 --> 00:15:31.700
Well, it's our problem. Don't worry about it.

00:15:43.560 --> 00:15:47.300
Sorry to wake you up like that,

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:52.090
but soon you'll have a tasty steak, Masayan.

00:15:57.410 --> 00:15:59.870
Now, where's this steak?

00:16:00.360 --> 00:16:03.870
It's over here. Look, a steak.

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:10.380
You can have this, too.

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:27.630
You fail at everything you do!

00:16:28.350 --> 00:16:29.250
Spineless wimp!

00:16:30.010 --> 00:16:33.130
That's right. Don't forget that feeling.

00:16:33.880 --> 00:16:36.890
I didn't think you'd come 
so far in such a short time.

00:16:47.240 --> 00:16:49.710
What?! You got rid of him?!

00:16:49.710 --> 00:16:51.570
You seemed to not know what to do with him.

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:54.710
Idiot! That doesn't mean 
you just drop him off in—

00:16:56.100 --> 00:16:57.400
What's wrong, Yamazaki?

00:16:57.400 --> 00:17:00.580
Let's go out and find Masayan right now!

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:05.080
Steakhouse
Beef

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:05.080
<b>Yakiniku</b>

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:05.080
<b>Hamburgers</b>

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:05.080
<b>Hearty 
Meats</b>

00:17:01.050 --> 00:17:03.570
<i>Yamazaki and Tonegawa begin a search,</i>

00:17:03.570 --> 00:17:06.950
<i>radiating outward from the location 
where Endou dumped Masayan,</i>

00:17:06.950 --> 00:17:09.590
<i>but there are no clues to be found!</i>

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:11.590
<b>Steakhouse Don</b>

00:17:12.130 --> 00:17:14.590
He has a round nose when 
viewed from the front,

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:16.720
but from the side, it's really angular...

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:20.690
He's an elderly man who eats steak 
barehanded and drools a lot!

00:17:20.690 --> 00:17:22.470
Did you see anyone like that?!

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:27.230
Come on, nobody like that actually exists!

00:17:27.230 --> 00:17:29.110
You bastard!

00:17:29.110 --> 00:17:31.480
Don't! Settle down, Yamazaki!

00:17:40.650 --> 00:17:43.270
Don't let it get you down so much, Yamazaki.

00:17:43.270 --> 00:17:48.440
But, sir, when I think about how 
Masayan might be out in this storm...

00:17:47.790 --> 00:17:51.860
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:17:52.970 --> 00:17:54.630
What is it, Yamazaki?

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:59.310
N-Nothing... I just thought 
I heard Masayan laughing.

00:18:00.850 --> 00:18:02.040
Masayan!

00:18:02.040 --> 00:18:04.520
Wait! Calm down, Yamazaki!

00:18:07.010 --> 00:18:09.060
Masayan!

00:18:10.210 --> 00:18:14.120
That's not Masayan! 
That's the actual president!

00:18:21.890 --> 00:18:24.920
Come on, Yamazaki. 
You don't want to get sick.

00:18:27.240 --> 00:18:30.170
Let's head back to my place.

00:18:35.940 --> 00:18:36.970
Damn it...

00:18:37.440 --> 00:18:39.320
You just had to butt in, didn't you?

00:18:40.820 --> 00:18:45.720
Handling the dirty work for you is part 
of my job description, Tonegawa-san.

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:56.360
I can hear him!

00:18:57.070 --> 00:18:58.490
What is it, Yamazaki?!

00:19:30.090 --> 00:19:33.730
Masayan... I'll never let you go again!

00:19:35.160 --> 00:19:36.480
Pointy-chin.

00:19:37.240 --> 00:19:40.220
Can't believe he walked all the way here...

00:19:43.720 --> 00:19:45.870
Please, Tonegawa-sensei!

00:19:47.670 --> 00:19:52.750
Please... Please let us 
keep Masayan at Teiai!

00:19:57.320 --> 00:19:58.330
We can't.

00:20:03.050 --> 00:20:08.040
Unless you're willing to take 
full responsibility for him, that is.

00:20:10.690 --> 00:20:14.360
Tonegawa-sensei, thank you so much!

00:20:19.960 --> 00:20:23.620
<i>And so, the tale of President 
Hyoudou's body double,</i>

00:20:22.920 --> 00:20:24.910
Masayan!

00:20:23.620 --> 00:20:28.330
<i>after many twists and turns, 
came to a conclusion.</i>

00:20:35.730 --> 00:20:37.630
You sure about this?

00:20:37.630 --> 00:20:39.000
It's insurance.

00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:39.590
Insurance?

00:20:40.490 --> 00:20:43.840
Think about it. There's no guarantee 
the president's interest

00:20:45.050 --> 00:20:47.600
in body doubles won't be piqued again.

00:20:49.240 --> 00:20:53.260
<i>Hang in there, Tonegawa! 
Don't give up, Tonegawa!</i>

00:20:53.720 --> 00:20:58.450
<i>This is the story of a lone man who struggles 
between his employer, the president,</i>

00:20:58.450 --> 00:21:02.790
<i>and his own employees, the men in black...</i>

00:21:02.790 --> 00:21:06.110
<i>Tonegawa Yukio: Middle Manager!</i>

00:21:06.470 --> 00:21:10.620
Well, since you're here again, 
I'm gonna need that money back.

00:21:11.640 --> 00:21:12.860
Ow!

00:21:13.200 --> 00:21:15.790
<b>Punishment</b>

00:21:13.450 --> 00:21:15.070
Punishment.

00:21:15.480 --> 00:21:17.530
Yeah! Yeah!

00:21:17.530 --> 00:21:20.090
<i>And Masayan stays at Teiai.</i>

00:22:55.410 --> 00:22:57.630
Next time, "Setting Sail."

00:22:56.370 --> 00:23:00.500
<b>Setting Sail</b>
